extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 39 (cache p040, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the cache and checked against a render of the whole page. The entry starts at The Filidh O.C.C., Herbalist & Bard heading and ends at Cybernetics & Bionics at the foot of the page. || GROUP: under The Woodland Druids (printed 38), one of its three orders; the book calls the druids practitioners of magic with a P.P.E. base, so occ_group is magic; it states no S.D.C. base, so men_of_arms is false. || XP: the column headed Herbalist, Woodland Druids, Blood Druids on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render; a note there names the Woodland Druids as the Dryad, Filidh and Scathach. Every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: hit points not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s other O.C.C.s. P.P.E. P.E. x2, +1D6+3 per level. || BONUSES: +4 vs faerie magic, foods and drinks (faerie_magic); +4 vs poisons and unwanted magic potions and foods (toxins_poisons); +1 vs all other types of magic, stored on spell_magic and ritual_magic; +4 vs horror factor. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Mystic Herbology is the row of printed 22 (+10%). Pilot: Horsemanship is Horsemanship: General; Pilot: Sailboat is Boat: Sail Type; Lore: Faerie is Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic; Tracking is Tracking (people). English and Faerie Speak have no language rows and share one Language: Other line at the printed 70% (row ruling, 2026-11-12: no language skill rows); Euro and Gobblely have rows; literacy in English rides a one-pick Literacy: Other group at +20%. The two ancient and two modern W.P.s are one pick of four, as the catalog does not separate them. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts may become Assassin if evil, no price printed: costs { assassin: 0 }. Pilot any is read to include the Horsemanship category at +5%. || EQUIPMENT: one wand and one staff of choice, offered from the held Millennium wand-of-* and staff-of-* rows (printed 19-22, cited to Japan) and the herb-magic wands and staves (cited to the Book of Magic); 12 of the 12+1D4 magic herbs or herb items, from every held herb-* row, the 1D4 by hand. Not stored: 1D4 wood throwing sticks (no row), common healing herbs, and magical bark or medium synthetic armor (traditional, not issued). Rope or cord is stored as nylon cord; pouches or sacks as one pouch."
