# Filidh

## Lore

The Filidh (pronounced fil leed) are the prophets, scholars, philosophers and healers of England''s woodland druids, in many respects bards. They study life and spread what they learn through word, story, song and dance, with a focus on the supernatural and on healing with herbs. Each is an expert herbalist and a warrior against evil supernatural forces, and many have learned to use radios, computers, cameras, blasters and vehicles.

Their herb magic is limited to divination, clairvoyance and protection against the supernatural: seeing the future and the other psychic gifts that warn of danger or give guidance come from special or magic herbs. Many are friends of the Millennium tree and receive visions, blankets of healing and the occasional Millennium wand from it.

## GM Notes

Clothing is stylish and practical, often Robin Hood style, with high boots, soft leather gloves, ornate medallions and jewelry in cheerful, warm colors. Many wear magical bark armor from the Millennium tree or medium synthetic armor. Starting kit beyond the sheet: 1D4 wood throwing sticks and common healing herbs. A Filidh is likely to acquire a second or third horse as pack animals and alternate rides.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'filidh');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'filidh';

